Changes for 2.0-0 (2026-11-27)
  * getParamCoef()/tauFetch(): generalized to also handle a yde-fitted borm() object, not just blrm()'s own pppo/cppo mechanism (per Frank's request, following the terminology review below). getParamCoef()'s what='betas'/'taus' split now computes the number of tau columns as qyde*ncol(ytransmat) for a borm() fit (myde is never stored, so it is rebuilt the same way bormPredictYde()/bormStats() already do), instead of only ever checking blrm()'s own pppo field (which borm() doesn't have, so what='taus' on a borm() fit previously always incorrectly stopped with "not a partial prop. odds model" even when taus were present). tauFetch() now detects a yde-fitted borm() object and delegates to a new internal helper, bormTauFetch() -- the borm() analog of tauFetch()'s own constrained-PPO branch: for each posterior draw, the qyde x myde Tau matrix is weighted by ytransmat at the requested intercept's Y level, giving one weighted-tau value per yde predictor per draw (borm()'s analog of blrm()'s cppo(y)*tau); borm() has no unconstrained-PPO analog, so only one branch is needed, unlike tauFetch()'s own two for blrm(). Also fixed, found while verifying this (a general, pre-existing R indexing gotcha, not borm-specific, but newly relevant since a borm() fit with one yde predictor and a single-column ytrans -- the common case -- has exactly one tau parameter): getParamCoef()'s what='taus'/'betas' silently dropped the result's names whenever exactly one parameter matched, since indexing a matrix with a single row AND a single column collapses to an unnamed scalar in base R. Verified: getParamCoef()'s betas+taus together exactly reconstruct what='both' with matching names; tauFetch()'s 'tau' output cross-checked directly against a hand-computed Tau %*% ytransmat[row,] for a specific posterior draw (exact match) and confirmed to vary correctly across different requested intercepts; blrm's own pppo-based behavior for both functions is unchanged (regression-tested); existing borm-yde.r/borm-orm.r/borm-blrm.r/blrm-contrast.r/blrm-pcontrast.r tests all pass; R CMD check --as-cran clean.
  * borm()/predict.borm()/Quantile.borm()/rms::Predict(): added type="quantile" for a yde-fitted borm() object, completing parity with rms::orm()'s own new type='quantile' (see rms's NEWS, 2026-11-25) -- the one orm() yde feature borm() was still missing. Requires q= (the quantile, e.g. .5 for the median); supports posterior.summary='mean'/'median'/'all' and an HPD interval via cint, the same per-posterior-draw-then-summarize pattern type='mean' already uses (there is no single MLE to run a delta method on, unlike orm()). The per-draw cumulative-probability-curve inversion was factored out of what was bormYdeQuantile()'s own inline code into a new shared helper, bormYdeInvertP(), callable once per draw. bormYdeQuantile() (the closure returned by Quantile() on a yde fit) is now a thin wrapper around predict(type='quantile'), the same division of labor bormYdeMean() already uses for type='mean' -- this changes its point estimate (cint=0, posterior.summary='mean', the default): it used to be the quantile of the posterior-MEAN probability curve (inverted once); it is now the posterior mean of each draw's OWN quantile (inverted once per draw, then averaged) -- confirmed by direct comparison that the two are close but not numerically identical, as expected from Jensen's inequality (inverting a cdf is a nonlinear operation). rms::Predict()'s fun='quantile' (added 2026-11-25 for orm() only) now also works for a yde-fitted borm() object, using bormPredictYde()'s HPD interval directly (no zcrit*se conversion needed, same as its existing fun='mean' handling there). Verified: point estimates agree exactly between Quantile()/predict()/Predict() for the same model; vector q is supported and monotone increasing within each row; method='discrete' and posterior.summary='median'/'all' all dispatch correctly; an ordinary (non-yde) borm() fit and rms::Predict() on other fit types still give clear errors instead of silently misbehaving; confirmed fun='mean' for Predict() on a yde-fitted borm() object already worked correctly before this change (an explicit ask, verified rather than assumed); existing borm-yde.r/borm-orm.r/borm-blrm.r regression tests all pass unchanged; R CMD check --as-cran clean on both rms and rmsb. Audited the rest of rms::orm()'s yde feature set against borm()'s own (fitted/fitted.ind/mean/ExProb/Survival/survest) and found no other gaps: ExProb()'s conf.int is unimplemented on both sides identically (not a borm-specific deficiency), and Survival.borm()/survest.borm() already handle yde fits (added 2026-11-23, see below).
  * borm(): naming consistency fixes with rms::orm(), per a cross-package audit of fit-object component names (2026-11-23): renamed the stored field ylevels to yunique (matching orm()'s own name for the same thing -- NOT backward compatible with previously-saved borm() fits, which must be refit); dropped the stored myde field entirely, now always recomputed as ncol(ytransmat) everywhere it's needed (matching orm()'s own convention of never storing it); dropped the redundant stored link field (always identical to family), with all borm-internal code now reading family directly; changed the yde tau coefficient name separator from " x " to " * " (e.g. "x2=b * yt1"), matching orm()'s own tauname convention exactly -- another non-backward-compatible, user-visible string change. bormBlrmDelegate() (used by predict.borm()/Mean.borm()/Quantile.borm()/ExProb.borm() for a non-yde fit's delegation to blrm.r's own generic methods) now also bridges ylevels/link onto the temporary delegate copy, since blrm.r's own code still expects those names unconditionally.
  * borm(): now stops with an informative error if yde/ytrans is given with only 1 modeled intercept (a binary Y) -- a Y-dependent effect is not meaningful with only one cutpoint, and would be exactly redundant with the main formula's own ordinary effect for that predictor. Matches an identical check added to rms::orm().
  * borm(): added the ytrans='all' shortcut, matching rms::orm()'s own (now k-1-free-parameter) version: one free tau parameter per modeled intercept except the first, which is anchored at zero for identifiability when the yde predictor is also in the main formula (the usual case). Does not support censored Y, and requires k <= 50 -- same restrictions as orm()'s own shortcut, for the same reasons. Verified against orm()'s own ytrans='all' MLE on identical data (coefficients agree to 3 significant figures between orm's MLE, borm's near-MLE optimizing mode, and borm's posterior mean), and against a loop-free vectorized construction's anchoring behavior via predict(..., ycut=) at both the anchored and a free cutpoint. While testing this, found and fixed a pre-existing, unrelated bug (confirmed with an ordinary custom ytrans too, not specific to 'all'): predict.borm()/bormStats() unconditionally re-parsed object$ytrans as deparsed text, which failed with "cannot coerce type 'closure' to vector of type 'character'" whenever object came from a file= cache hit, since borm() itself already re-hydrates a cache hit's ytrans into a real function before returning it.
  * print.borm()/print.blrm(): for non-plain (latex/html/typst) output,
    the point estimate in uncertainty-interval strings -- "point +/-
    se" and "point [lower, upper]" -- stays at normal size, while
    everything after it (the +/- symbol and se, or the brackets/comma-
    space and lower/upper, numbers included) renders in a smaller font
    via markupSpecs[[lang]]$smaller2. (Two earlier iterations: first
    only the +/- symbol/brackets/comma-space were smaller, leaving ALL
    numbers at normal size; then the whole string including the point
    estimate was made smaller2 -- both corrected per Frank's follow-up
    requests.) New shared helpers bormFmtPM()/bormFmtCI() (borm.r)
    replace the previous hand-rolled paste0() calls at all 4
    call sites (bormStats()/blrmStats()'s own text summaries, and
    print.borm()/print.blrm()'s sigma/LOO summaries); plain-text output
    is unaffected.
  * New function borm(): the Bayesian analog of rms::orm() (as blrm() is
    to rms::lrm()), supporting all 5 of orm()'s link families (logistic,
    probit, log-log, complementary log-log, Cauchy), exact censoring,
    pcontrast, and both the single- and dual-sigma (mix_re) random-
    intercept extensions of rms::orm.rfit(). Includes bormStats()/
    print.bormStats() for Spearman's rho and Somers' Dxy with highest
    posterior density intervals, following rms::orm()'s own censoring
    rules. See web/R/rmsb/borm_development.md for the full development
    history.
  * borm(): new yde/ytrans mechanism for Y-dependent
    (non-proportional-odds) effects, generalizing blrm()'s own ppo/cppo
    to allow more than one Y-dependent shape at once, with a combined
    beta+tau npcontrast for the Y-dependent effect. tausd, the prior SD
    for tau, is specified on a raw, portable scale -- one unit of the
    yde predictor, one SD of ytrans(y) -- rather than an internal,
    dataset-dependent one; default value unchanged.
  * print.borm()'s summary table reorganized: first column now shows
    Obs, Distinct Y, Median Y, p, Draws, Chains, Time (plus cluster/
    random-effect information when present); third column shows the
    mean |P(Y>=median)-0.5| index, matching rms::print.orm(), including
    its subscripted Y[0.5] formatting under prType='latex'/'html'.
  * blrm()/borm(): new cores_loo argument (default 1) to control loo()'s
    own parallelism separately from the mc.cores option; "loo failed"
    now reports the actual underlying error instead of a generic message.
  * blrm()/borm(): sampling.args's documentation now describes using
    adapt_delta/max_treedepth to address divergent transitions on hard,
    separation-prone data.
  * blrm(): fixed a bug where a user-supplied init= was silently ignored
    when backend='rstan'.
  * blrm(): Stan code now uses precomputed censoring subscripts from
    rms::ormIdx() (shared with borm()); fixed two related bugs found in
    the process -- a stale censoring-sentinel convention that could
    silently break censored fits, and a cppo left-censoring score that
    did not vary with the censoring bound.
  * blrm(): the unconstrained PPO model (ppo without cppo) with censored
    Y now errors informatively instead of silently corrupting the
    response.
  * blrm(): Ncens1/Ncens2 (matching rms::orm.fit()'s own convention)
    replace the old Ncens field in the fit object and in print.blrm() --
    not backward compatible with fits saved before this change.
  * blrm(): npcontrast's ycut argument now actually has an effect (was
    previously silently ignored); ycut may also be a named vector giving
    a different Y value per named setting.
  * blrm(): normcppo=TRUE now prints a warning when used with cppo,
    since it can distort the ordinary (non-PPO) coefficient for any
    predictor that also appears in the main formula.
  * blrm(): improved numerical accuracy of the interior/interval-censored
    log-likelihood terms in the constrained- and unconstrained-PPO Stan
    code.
  * DESCRIPTION: now requires rms >= 8.2-2.
  * borm(): tau coefficient names for yde now use ytrans's own column
    names when available and unique, otherwise generic names yt (one
    column) or yt1, yt2, ... (more than one column).
  * borm(): predict() now supports type='fitted', 'fitted.ind', and
    'mean' for a fit using yde/ytrans (previously only type='lp'/'x'
    were supported); also fixed a bug where type='mean' was not
    accepted by predict.borm() at all, even for an ordinary (non-yde)
    fit.
  * borm(): Mean(), Quantile(), and ExProb() now work for a fit using
    yde/ytrans (previously errored); for such a fit the function they
    return must be called with newdata= (a data frame) instead of a
    bare linear predictor, since a Y-dependent effect cannot be
    represented by a single linear predictor value.
  * blrm(): fixed a bug where predict(type='mean') was listed as a
    valid option but crashed when used, for an ordinal (more than 2
    response levels) fit.
  * borm(): Quantile() for a fit using yde/ytrans now also supports
    method='interpolated' (previously only 'discrete'), and is now the
    default, matching rms::Quantile.orm().
  * borm(): ExProb() for a fit using yde/ytrans now gives an informative
    error for conf.int= (not yet implemented) instead of silently
    ignoring it and returning a result with no interval.
  * New Survival.borm()/survest.borm(), the Bayesian analogs of
    rms::Survival.orm()/survest.orm(), fully accounting for posterior
    uncertainty: survival probabilities (and their highest posterior
    density intervals, when requested) are computed separately for each
    posterior draw, then summarized across draws. Works for ordinary
    borm() fits and for fits using yde/ytrans. Requires y=TRUE (the
    default) when the fit was made. Unlike rms::Survival.orm(), always
    requires newdata (no bare linear-predictor/design-matrix
    alternative, since no single value represents every posterior
    draw). A highest posterior density interval, or
    posterior.summary='median', needs every posterior draw's value at
    every requested time stored at once; when that would need more than
    hpd_threshold (default 1.5e7) total values, this stops with an
    informative error instead of attempting it -- specify fewer times=,
    or use the default posterior.summary='mean' with conf.int=0 for a
    cheap running-mean result unaffected by this limit.

Changes for 1.1-3 (2026-10-29)
   * blrm: added sampling.args to hash digest
   * print.blrm: changed to use new version of prModFit in rms
   * print.rmsb: fixed old bug related to rownames being lost with drop=TRUE which surfaced with one predictor and intercepts=FALSE
   * cluster: removed this function as it is now in the new, required rms package

Changes for 1.1-2 (2025-04-13)
   * predict.blrm: fixed type='fitted' for binary Y; thanks Christian Hametner: <https://discourse.datamethods.org/t/bayesian-regression-modeling-strategies/6105/99>
   * removed Ocens function which is now in rms 7.0
   * changed to be compatible with storage of functions in rms::probabilityFamilies
   * updated to use Ocens2ord on top of Ocens, needs rms 8.0-0

Changes for 1.1-1 (2024-07-07)
   * blrm: added argument showopt to show Stan optimizer steps, default is FALSE
   * blrm: added options(rmsbmsg=FALSE) to allow the user to suppress information messages
   * lrmconppot.stan: fixed bug for dim(C2) p -> q
   * replaced use of survival::survConcordance and Hmisc::somers2 with concordancefit

Changes for 1.1-0 (2024-03-11)
   * Store cppo as deparsed for opt object from optimization (MLE) to prevent huge environment from being carried along
   * blrm: Non-downward compatible changes: removed keepsep argument
   * blrm: Added npcontrast argument for specification of priors for non-proportional-odds parameters in the constrained partial PO model through the use of contrasts, parallel to pcontrast for the PO part of the model; changed 3 stan code modules for this

Changes for 1.0-0 (2023-09-26)
   * blrm: added support for cmdstan and cmdstanr package using backend=
   * When using cmdstan uses bayesplot package for pairs plots
   * stanDx: new code for cmdstan diagnostics
   * stackMI: corrected erroneous implementation of file= where it was only applying to one of the imputations; also handled generally the conversion of functions in fit object to character strings for efficient serializing
   * Added non-exported function cluster so as to not depend on survival package
   * blrm: added sampling.args argument
   * blrm: trapped ppairs error in case plot region too small to hold graph
   * blrm: added pcontrast argument for user-specified priors on linear combinations of regression coefficients; required changing all Stan code
   * blrm: removed priorsd argument (NON-DOWNWARD-COMPATIBLE CHANGE)

Changes for 0.1-0 (2022-04-12)
   * blrm: got around bug in model.response not keeping class Ocens
   * soprobMarkovOrdPost: removed since Hmisc has soprobMarkovOrdm
   * lrmconppot.stan: removed redundant pi simplex (thanks Mark Jones <mark.jones1@sydney.edu.au>

Changes for 0.0-2 (2021-02-27)
   * Removed @title lines from Roxygen comments
   * Enhanced predict.blrm and changed prediction methods to use it
   * Changed storage of cppo function in fit object to character strings so as to not have saveRDS serialize it with all its environment data
   * Added lrmconppot.stan to implement flat and t-distribution priors for intercepts
   * blrm: added iprior argument for lrmconppot
   * predict.blrm: fixed fun= with finint=FALSE
